.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH sway-things-screenshot 1 "" "Sway Things 0.6.0" "Sway Things Manual"
.SH NAME
sway\-things\-screenshot \- Take a screenshot with grim, and save and copy it as the Screenshots & Clipboard page says; the screenshot keys run this
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsway\-things screenshot\fR [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIAREA\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Take a screenshot with grim, and save and copy it as the Screenshots & Clipboard page says; the screenshot keys run this
.PP
The folder, the file name pattern, whether the picture is saved, copied or both, and what follows (a notification with Open and Edit, or the editor) come from the settings. A selection canceled with Escape takes no picture and is no error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
Controls when to use color
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIAREA\fR>
What to capture: a region you select (or a window you click) with slurp, the focused window, the focused display or all displays
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
region: A region you select, or a window you click
.IP \(bu 2
window: The focused window
.IP \(bu 2
display: The display with the focus
.IP \(bu 2
all: Every display
.RE
